@startuml
!include ../common/style.puml

title HANBAY HOTEL - Payment State Machine

hide empty description

[*] --> PENDING : create payment attempt

state PENDING
state SUCCESS
state FAILED
state REFUNDED

PENDING --> SUCCESS : verified success webhook\n[idempotency check passed]
PENDING --> FAILED : gateway reports failure
PENDING --> FAILED : payment request expires
PENDING --> FAILED : verification rejected

SUCCESS --> REFUNDED : refund completed\n[cancellation/refund approved]

FAILED --> [*] : no retry / booking cancelled
REFUNDED --> [*]
SUCCESS --> [*] : payment lifecycle closed\n[no refund requested]

SUCCESS --> SUCCESS : duplicate success webhook\n[ignore safely]
FAILED --> FAILED : duplicate failure webhook\n[ignore safely]
REFUNDED --> REFUNDED : duplicate refund callback\n[ignore safely]

note right of PENDING
  The payment request has been created,
  but no verified final result exists.
end note

note right of SUCCESS
  The booking may transition from
  PENDING to CONFIRMED only once.
end note

note right of FAILED
  A failed attempt does not necessarily
  cancel the booking immediately.
  A retry creates a new Payment attempt
  while the booking remains payable.
end note

note right of REFUNDED
  Refunding does not directly define the
  booking state; the booking cancellation
  policy controls that transition.
end note

legend bottom
  == Reliability rules ==
  - transactionRef or gateway eventId must be unique.
  - Every callback must be verified before changing state.
  - Repeated callbacks must not duplicate booking confirmation or refund.
  - A success received after booking expiration must be handled explicitly.
endlegend

@enduml
